; Frame cards in, each parameter's start and step out. A frame is 13 cards: V (1 voiced, 0 not), P (the pitch
; period in samples), A (the excitation amplitude) and K10 down to K1 (each reflection coefficient times 1000). A
; card below zero ends the frames. For each frame it sends V, then for P, A and each K the frame's value and the
; step to the next frame's, (next - this) / 10 by SFT 01. When V changes there is no glide: the step is 0, by SFT 04.
; The frame in hand is kept on cards: it goes round through this machine's own pile (the host routes OUT at 07 and
; 35 back to INP at 28 and 47), so the machine needs no array.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            start   INP   cv       03-12: the first frame: V here, the rest onto the pile
  04                    CLA   n11
  05                    STO   i
  06            first   INP   x
  07                    OUT   x
  08                    CLA   i
  09                    SUB   00
  10                    STO   i
  11                    TAC   frame
  12                    JMP   first
  13            frame   INP   nv       13-23: the next frame's V: the end, a glide (SFT 01) or none (SFT 04)
  14                    CLA   nv
  15                    TAC   end
  16                    SUB   cv
  17                    TAC   diff
  18                    SUB   00
  19                    TAC   same
  20            diff    CLA   s404
  21                    JMP   set
  22            same    CLA   s401
  23            set     STO   sft
  24                    OUT   cv       24-43: V, then each value and its step; the next frame goes on the pile
  25                    CLA   n11
  26                    STO   i
  27            each    INP   x
  28                    INP   c
  29                    OUT   c
  30                    CLA   x
  31                    SUB   c
  32            sft     DATA  0        (SFT 01 or SFT 04)
  33                    STO   d
  34                    OUT   d
  35                    OUT   x
  36                    CLA   i
  37                    SUB   00
  38                    STO   i
  39                    TAC   next
  40                    JMP   each
  41            next    CLA   nv
  42                    STO   cv
  43                    JMP   frame
  44            end     OUT   cv       44-55: the last frame, its steps 0
  45                    CLA   n11
  46                    STO   i
  47            last    INP   c
  48                    OUT   c
  49                    OUT   z
  50                    CLA   i
  51                    SUB   00
  52                    STO   i
  53                    TAC   done
  54                    JMP   last
  55            done    HRS   00
  60            cv      DATA  0
  61            nv      DATA  0
  62            x       DATA  0
  63            c       DATA  0
  64            d       DATA  0
  65            i       DATA  0
  66            z       DATA  0
  67            n11     DATA  11
  68            s401    SFT   01
  69            s404    SFT   04
